   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d665e7">
         <p>Consider a Normal paragraph that contains a mix of bold, italic, and monospace (Courier New or Consolas) formatting applied to individual words or phrases.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Paragraph with mixed character styles</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>.docx Style / Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>The <b>Management Console</b> uses the config.yaml file to control advanced system behavior.</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_jcb_1xw_jkc">
&lt;p>
  The &lt;b>Management Console&lt;/b> uses the &lt;codeph>config.yaml&lt;/codeph> file to control &lt;i>advanced&lt;/i> system behavior.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>
            <b>Result:</b>The converter preserves all inline formatting within a single paragraph <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph>. For a full list of character style mappings, see the Character Styles section.</p>
      </section>
   </refbody>
